    </div></div>
                        


        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="cfedContent">
        
        <div class="cfedContent__body">
            
<h2>References</h2>                <div class="cfedContent__text"><p>Bernanke, Ben S., 2012, <a title="press conference" href="http://federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20120425.pdf" target="_blank">press conference</a>, Board of the Governors of the Federal Reserve System, Washington, DC,&nbsp;April 25.</p>

<p>Cardarelli, Roberto, and Alessandro Rebucci, 2007, &ldquo;<a title="Exchange rates and the adjustment of external imbalances" href="http://www.imf.org/external/pubs/ft/weo/2007/01/pdf/c3.pdf" target="_blank">Exchange rates and the adjustment of external imbalances</a>,&rdquo; in World Economic Outlook, Washington DC: International Monetary Fund, April, pp. 81&ndash;120.</p>

<p>Congressional Budget Office, 2012, "Economic effects of reducing the fiscal restraint that is scheduled to occur in 2013," <a title="report" href="http://www.cbo.gov/sites/default/files/cbofiles/attachments/FiscalRestraint_0.pdf" target="_blank">report</a>, Washington, DC, May.</p>

<p>Crane, Leland, Meredith Crowley and Saad Quayyum, 2007, &ldquo;<a title="Understanding the evolution of trade deficits: Trade elasticities of industrialized countries" href="/-/media/publications/economic-perspectives/2007/ep-4qtr2007-part1-crane-etal-pdf.pdf" target="_self">Understanding the evolution of trade deficits: Trade elasticities of industrialized countries</a>,&rdquo; <em>Economic Perspectives</em>, Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago, Vol. 31, Fourth Quarter, pp. 2&ndash;17.</p>

<p>Eggertsson, Gauti B., and Michael Woodford, 2003, &ldquo;The zero bound on interest rates and optimal monetary policy,&rdquo; <em>Brookings Papers on Economic Activity</em>, Vol. 34, No. 1, pp. 139&ndash;211.</p>

<p>Krugman, Paul R., 1998, &ldquo;It&rsquo;s baaack: Japan&rsquo;s slump and the return of the liquidity trap,&rdquo; <em>Brookings Papers on Economic Activity</em>, Vol. 29, No. 2, pp. 137&ndash;206.</p>

<p>International Monetary Fund, Research Department, 2012, "Growth resuming, dangers remain," <em>World Economic Outlook: April 2012</em>,&nbsp;<a title="report" href="http://www.imf.org/external/pubs/ft/weo/2012/01/pdf/text.pdf" target="_blank">report</a>, Washington DC, April 17.</p>

<p>Reifschneider, David L., and John C. Williams, 2000, &ldquo;Three lessons for monetary policy in a low inflation era,&rdquo; <em>Journal of Money, Credit and Banking</em>, Vol. 32, No. 4, November, pp. 936&ndash;966.</p>

<p>Reinhart, Carmen M., and Kenneth S. Rogoff, 2009, <em>This Time is Different: Eight Centuries of Financial Folly</em>, Princeton, NJ: Princeton University Press.</p>

<p>Taylor, John B., 1993, &ldquo;Discretion versus policy rules in practice,&rdquo; <em>Carnegie-Rochester Conference Series on Public Policy</em>, Vol. 39, No. 1, December, pp.195&ndash;214.</p>

<p>Werning, Ivan, 2011, &ldquo;Managing a liquidity trap: Monetary and fiscal policy,&rdquo; National Bureau of Economic Research, working paper, No. 17344, August.</p>

<p>Yellen, Janet L., 2012, &ldquo;The economic outlook and monetary policy,&rdquo; <a title="speech" href="http://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/yellen20120411a.htm" target="_blank">speech</a>, Money Marketeers of New York University, New York, April 11.</p></div>
                        


        </div>
